  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-12-01T22:00:10.435Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Pretty simple, I wonder if it would be possible to set an FPS threshold bellow which avatars start culling/ turning off. I've been crashed quite a few times in the last week, and while ONCE I was able to save myself by pressing all the buttons to enable safe mode it took a LONG time to register the input.\n\nBut if the game could automatically start culling the most performance intensive avatars (not worn by friends) as FPS drops, it may get a chance to cull an offending avatar before it generates enough particles or whatever to actually crash people.\n\nThis could also be beneficial server side as particularly if each players system culls different avatars first, it would make it easier to pinpoint which avatar caused the crash.\n\nIt would also help with non-crasher that still cause significant performance hits, as fps drops tend to be the main cause of motion sickness for most players.",
